silm:instances_papers_05_granite_substrate_chapters_02_typed_materialization_sections_01_chunk_typing_concrete_anchor a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "ChunkTypingConcreteAnchorExample" .
silm:instances_papers_05_granite_substrate_chapters_02_typed_materialization_sections_01_chunk_typing_concrete_anchor silm:hasExample "In 'ChunkTypingConcreteAnchor', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, the leg-type label \"evidence\" assigned to the Tartu vet-record chunk — it is an information artifact about Mittens, not a classification or quality measurement; also, the content-addressed hash sha256:7f4a... uniquely identifying the Tartu vet-record payload (patient: Mittens, date: 2026-05-18, vet: Dr. Tamm, body mass: 4.3 kg, vaccinations: up to date); also, the SHACL-compatible shape predicate VetRecordShape requiring fields: patient name, date, attending veterinarian, body-mass measurement, vaccination status." .
